    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule is present.",
    "No matched oral-versus-intravenous exposure data for the query are available.",
    "First-pass metabolism, transporter involvement, and formulation effects for the query are not directly characterized.",
    "Species differences between mouse and human and formulation dependence in the reference contexts limit quantitative transfer."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L2 records from the same contexts reinforce the L1 picture: every measured oral bioavailability value in the visible transferable contexts is at or above 20 percent, with central estimates mostly 24 to 92 percent. The only low-sounding statements are relative comparisons such as thiocolchicoside versus intramuscular or variability ranges such as didanosine 2 to 89 percent, whose central estimates remain above threshold. No affirmative evidence supports F below 20 percent for the query, so the high prediction is retained and modestly strengthened."
}

